### Prototype Evolution
* **Initial Concept:** Designed a fully parametric model in Onshape using FeatureScript ("HAVF profile generator") with independent variables for root width, pitch, backbone offset, and profile thickness[cite: 2]. Evaluated airflows digitally using a custom CFD web simulator (`aerofoil-simulation/index.html`) before printing[cite: 2].
* **Version A1:** Root width $25\text{ mm}$, backbone offset $8\text{ mm}$[cite: 2].
  * *Testing:* Placed on fan test rig[cite: 2].
  * *Outcome:* Failed to rotate[cite: 2].
  * *Analysis:* Root chord was too narrow to generate the torque needed to overcome internal motor cogging and bearing resistance[cite: 2].
* **Version B1:** Scaled root width to $60\text{ mm}$, backbone offset to $20\text{ mm}$, profile thickness $2\text{ mm}$[cite: 2].
  * *Testing:* Spun freely under no-load conditions ($63\text{ RPM}$), but RPM dropped to $30\text{ RPM}$ under generator load[cite: 2].
* **Version C1:** Kept root width at $60\text{ mm}$, increased profile thickness to $4\text{ mm}$[cite: 2].
  * *Testing:* Lower free-running speed ($60\text{ RPM}$), but maintained much higher loaded speed ($49\text{ RPM}$)[cite: 2]. The thicker profile improved low-speed torque transfer[cite: 2].
* **Version D1 (Final Model):** Expanded root width to $80\text{ mm}$, adjusted thickness back to $2\text{ mm}$ to reduce mass while preserving blade surface area[cite: 2].
  * *Testing:* Maintained high loaded RPM ($49\text{ RPM}$) and generated the first measurable multimeter readings ($0.01\text{ V}$, $0.04\text{ A}$)[cite: 2].

