## 11. Failure and Debugging

### Case Study: Version A1 Rotation Failure
* **Symptom:** Blade A1 remained completely stationary when exposed to airflow up to $3.5\text{ m/s}$[cite: 2].
* **Investigation:** Measured the root width ($25\text{ mm}$) and backbone offset ($8\text{ mm}$)[cite: 2]. Tested the generator shaft independently to confirm there were no mechanical blockages.
* **Root Cause:** The $25\text{ mm}$ root chord did not capture enough airflow force to overcome static friction and motor magnet cogging[cite: 2].
* **Resolution:** Modified the parametric CAD variables to expand the root width to $60\text{ mm}$ (Version B1)[cite: 2].
* **Verification:** Version B1 rotated smoothly upon airflow exposure, reaching $63\text{ RPM}$ unloaded[cite: 2].

